==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|ru|:inh|orv:по}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|по}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*po}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{ru-IPA|pɐ}} {{q|before a stressed syllable}}
* {{ru-IPA|по́}} {{q|when stressed}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-по.ogg}}

===Preposition===
{{head|ru|preposition}}

# {{+obj|ru|dat|catpos=prep}}
## {{n-g|used broadly to indicate action, typically involving movement, across a surface or across several things in a generally flat plane}}; [[across]], [[on]], [[along]], [[down]], [[up]], [[all over]], ([[all around|all]]) [[around]]:
##: {{uxi|ru|[[таракан|Тарака́н]] [[бе́гал]] '''по''' [[столу́]].|The cockroach ran '''across''' the table.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[плыл]] '''по''' [[реке́]].|t=He swam '''down''' the river.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[путеше́ствовали]] '''по''' [[Европа|Евро́пе]].|They travelled '''around''' Europe.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[путеше́ствовали]] '''по''' [[разный|ра́зным]] [[города́м]].|They travelled '''around''' different cities.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[погла́дил]] [[меня́]] '''по''' [[щеке́]].|He stroked my cheek. / He stroked me '''on'''/'''across''' the cheek.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[уда́рили]] [[меня́]] '''по''' [[голове́]].|They hit me '''on'''/'''over'''/'''across''' the head.}}
## {{n-g|used to indicate the object/field/topic that something applies to}}; [[for]], [[on]], [[about]], [[in]], [[of]] (''or translated with an attributive noun followed by a noun'')
##: {{uxi|ru|[[министерство|Министе́рство]] '''по''' [[чрезвычайный|чрезвыча́йным]] [[ситуа́циям]] ([[МЧС]])|The Ministry '''of''' Emergency Situations (MChS)}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[руково́дство]] '''по''' [[шитью́]]|sewing guide / guide '''to'''/'''for'''/'''on''' sewing}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[рекоменда́ции]] '''по''' [[устране́нию]] [[угро́з]]|recommendations to eliminate threats / recommendations '''for'''/'''on''' eliminating threats}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[экза́мен]] '''по''' [[биоло́гии]]|biology exam|lit=exam '''on'''/'''in'''/'''for''' biology}}
## {{n-g|used to indicate accordance with, adherence to or judgement based on something}}; [[according to]], [[from]], [[by]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[су́дя]] '''по''' [[его́]] [[поведе́нию]]|judging '''from''' his behaviour}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[по́нял]] [[э́то]] '''по''' [[его́]] [[го́лосу]].|I could tell '''by'''/'''from''' his voice.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|'''по''' [[пла́ну]]|'''according''' to plan}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[де́йствовать]] '''по''' [[пра́вилам]]|to act '''according''' to / '''in accordance/line with''' the rules}}
##: {{syn|ru|согла́сно<q:partial>}}
## {{n-g|used to indicate the reason for something, typically undesired/undesirable (see usage notes on {{m|ru|из-за}})}}; [[due to]], [[on account of]], [[out of]], [[from]], [[by]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[ушёл]] [[на]] [[пе́нсию]] [[по]] [[боле́зни]].|He retired '''due to''' illness.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[Аро́н]] [[вчера́]] [[опозда́л]] '''по''' [[рассе́янности]].|Aaron was late yesterday '''because of''' a distraction.}}
##: {{syn|ru|из-за}}
##* {{quote-book|ru|year=1958|author=w:ru:[[Ефремов, Иван Антонович|Иван Ефремов]]<t:{{w|Ivan Yefremov}}>|title=w:ru:[[Туманность Андромеды (роман)|Туманность Андромеды]]|chapter=Глава II. Эпсилон Тукана|location=Москва|publisher=w:ru:[[Молодая гвардия (издательство)|Молодая гвардия]]|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:[[George Hanna (translator)|George Hanna]]|title2=w:Andromeda: A Space-Age Tale|location2=Moscow|publisher2=w:[[Foreign Languages Publishing House (Soviet Union)|Foreign Languages Publishing House]]|year2=1959|page2=|pageurl2=|text=Когда́ челове́чество перешло́ на еди́ный алфави́т, на́званный лине́йным '''по''' отсу́тствию сло́жных зна́ков, фильмова́ние да́же ста́рых книг ста́ло ещё бо́лее просты́м и досту́пным автомати́ческим маши́нам.|t=When all mankind adopted a single alphabet – it was called the linear alphabet '''because''' there were no complicated signs in it – it became easy to film even the old books, so that eventually the process was fully mechanized.}}
## {{n-g|used with time (usually times of day or days of the week) to indicate regular repetition}}; [[on]], [[in]] (the), [[every]] (''or translated with a plural noun'')
##: {{uxi|ru|'''по''' [[четверга́м]]|t=('''on''') Thursdays / '''every''' Thursday}}
##: {{uxi|ru|'''по''' [[вечера́м]]|t=evenings / '''every''' evening}}
##: {{syn|ru|ка́ждый}}
## {{n-g|used with numbers when there is distribution among multiple objects or repetition across multiple instances in time ({{lg|dative case}} is used with the numbers one, a thousand, a million, a billion, a trillion etc. and numbers ending in these words)}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[дал]] [[каждый|ка́ждому]] [[челове́ку]] '''по''' [[двадцати́ одному́]] [[рублю́]].|I gave each person twenty-one roubles.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[пла́вал]] [[ка́ждый]] [[день]] '''по''' [[ты́сяче]] [[ме́тров]].|He swam a thousand metres every day.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[продаю́т]] '''по''' [[миллио́ну]] [[альбо́мов]] [[в]] [[год]].|They sell a million albums a year.}}
# {{+obj|ru|acc|catpos=prep}}
## {{n-g|used with numbers when there is distribution among multiple objects or repetition across multiple instances in time ({{lg|inanimate}} {{lg|accusative case|accusative}} case is used with numbers other than one, a thousand, a million, a billion, a trillion etc. or numbers ending in these words)}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[бы́ли]] [[разделённый|разделены́]] [[на]] [[гру́ппы]] '''по''' [[три]] [[челове́ка]].|They were divided into groups of three people.|source=Note: not the animate {{m|ru|трёх}}.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[получа́л]] '''по''' [[два́дцать пять]] [[фу́нтов]] [[в]] [[неде́лю]].|He received £25 a week.}}
## {{n-g|Used to indicate something serving as the boundary of the extent of some action.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[всади́л]] [[в]] [[ружьё]] [[штык]] '''по''' [[са́мое]] [[дуло|ду́ло]].|I stuck a bayonet into a gun '''to''' the very barrel.}}
##: {{syn|ru|до}}
# {{+obj|ru|pre|catpos=prep}}
## {{lb|ru|literary|[[official#English|official]]}} {{n-g|Used to indicate a temporal or spatial boundary}}; (immediately) [[after]], [[upon]], [[on]]
##: {{uxi|ru|'''по''' [[прие́зде]]/[[прибы́тии]]|'''on'''/'''upon''' arrival}}
##: {{uxi|ru|'''по''' [[истече́нии]] [[полуго́да]]|'''after''' six months}}
##: {{syn|ru|по́сле<q:partial>}}
## to the [[liking]] of
##: {{uxi|ru|'''по''' [[нём]]|to his liking}}
# {{+obj|ru|pre/dat|catpos=prep}}
## {{n-g|used to indicate an object of rumination, yearning, mourning}}; [[over]], [[for]]
##: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Он]] [[горева́л]] '''по''' [[моём]] [[отсу́тствии]].|He grieved ('''over''') my absence.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] [[сходи́ли]] '''по''' [[нём]] [[с]] [[ума́]].|They were going crazy '''for''' him.}}
##: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[скуча́ю]] '''по''' [[тебе́]].|I miss you.}}

====Usage notes====
* When used with numbers in the distributive meaning, the following should be noted:
** The case of any associated noun follows the normal case rules for numbers. This means full agreement when dative is used ({{m|ru|'''по''' [[одному́]] [[вопро́су]]}}) and genitive singular or plural (depending on the last digit) when accusative is used ({{m|ru|'''по''' [[три]] [[вопро́са]]}}, {{m|ru|'''по''' [[семь]] [[вопро́сов]]}}).
** With {{m|ru|два}}, {{m|ru|три}} and {{m|ru|сто}} (but not numbers ending in these numbers), the stress is optionally drawn onto '''по''':
**: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[дал]] [[им]] '''по́''' [[два]] / '''по''' [[два́]] [[рубля́]].|I gave them '''two''' roubles each.}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ru|по ме́ре того́ как}}

